# ReportIQ MCP and Feed

## Programmatic access (this repo’s MCP)

When the **reportiq** MCP server is enabled and the FastAPI app is up (`REPORTIQ_API_BASE`, default `http://127.0.0.1:8000`):

- Prefer **`reportiq_*` tools** (health, intake analyze, RAG, intake gaps) instead of ad-hoc `curl` for the same operations.
- Intake: pass non-empty `q1_text` and optional flat `form_data` (string keys) to `reportiq_intake_analyze`, matching `POST /api/questions/intake/analyze`.
- RAG: call `reportiq_rag_construct_sentence` then `reportiq_rag_policy_quote` with the same `form_data`; pass the constructed `sentence` into `reportiq_rag_policy_quote` as `constructed_sentence` when mirroring the app.
- Read field keys and conditionals: fetch the **resource** `reportiq://form-schema` (see [docs/MCP.md](docs/MCP.md)).

**Do not** expect these tools to list or read **Feed** submissions. The Feed is `localStorage` in the browser.

## Browser and Feed (cursor-ide-browser or manual)

- After **Submit** on the home form, a new row appears on **`/feed`**. There is no HTTP API for that list.
- To verify: open the app origin, use **browser_snapshot** before structural interactions, and after any navigation. Use **browser_lock** per the host’s instructions (lock before interactions when a tab already exists; navigate first if needed). After `browser_navigate` to `/feed`, take a new snapshot, expand the `SubmissionRow`, and check the **Report** and **Summary** tabs for AI extraction when the intake run succeeded.
- E2E checklist: fill all sections; handle conditionals (e.g. contact if not anonymous, supervisor who if “yes” to supervisor involved, evidence if “yes” to supporting materials, “if other, how” when relevant); in **AI follow-up** click **Generate AI follow-up**, wait for loading, complete **Next** on 0–2 follow-up questions, allow **construct** and **policy** steps, **Done** on the policy step, then **Submit**; navigate to **Feed** and expand the new row.

## When to use which

- **MCP (reportiq)**: headless health checks, intake and RAG against the **backend only**.
- **Browser MCP**: any flow that must touch **`localStorage`**, the full wizard UI, or **Feed** rows.
